    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d180">

                <pb facs="0409" n="397" sameAs="frus:frus1946v09/pg397"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">Marshall Mission Files, Lot 54–D270:
                    Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">General Marshall to
                        Colonel Paul R. M. Miller</hi><anchor n="24"
                        xml:id="d180-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">[<placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Chungking</hi></placeName>,] <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1946-02-08">8 February 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>166. Information in Chungking indicates that General Tseng Sheng is Commander of
                    Communist-led forces in the Canton area. He is supposedly located on Tapeng
                    Peninsula. Your team should proceed to the Tapeng Peninsula area and attempt
                    contact with General Tseng Sheng whose title is Commander of the Communist-led
                    Kwan[g]tung East River Detachment. Send report direct to the Executive
                    Headquarters as to conditions found in that area. Tapeng Peninsula is situated
                    between the Bias and the Mirs Bays.</p>
                <p>To Haskell:<anchor n="25" xml:id="d180-f2"/> Communists here indicate that they
                    would like to send signal personnel from Peiping to Canton to operate radio
                    station taken there by the Communists. Check this with Communists in Executive
                    Headquarters and if report is correct see that their personnel are sent to
                    Canton.</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d180-f1" n="24" type="source" xml:id="d180-f1-content">
                <p>Colonel Miller was American member and chairman of the Executive Headquarters’
                    Canton Liaison Group, Canton, Kwangtung.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d180-f2" n="25" xml:id="d180-f2-content">
                <p>Information copy sent by Brigadier General Byroade to his Chief of Staff in
                    Executive Headquarters at Peiping, Colonel L. W. Haskell.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
